interfaces = []
do_1 = "In storage/db_engine/litt/util/ssh.go:24 document Transfer as a finite inactivity bound, expose the existing SSHTimeouts options through NewSSHSession at :63 without breaking current callers, and change operation tracking at :206 and RsyncContext at :278 so healthy data progress is governed by the rsync inactivity timeout at :338 rather than a fixed whole-file deadline; preserve explicit caller deadlines, session cancellation, process-group termination and joining at :343, host verification at :325, and a separately bounded Command timeout for acknowledgeDurable at :356, without disabling a timeout or changing command-operation bounds. Existing push and sync callers at storage/db_engine/litt/cli/push.go:119 and storage/db_engine/litt/cli/sync.go:219 must inherit the corrected transfer policy without changing those files."
do_2 = "Add TestSSHSession_TransferProgressTimeout in storage/db_engine/litt/util/ssh_test.go using the real receiver from storage/db_engine/litt/util/repair_114_test.go:275 and shortened configurable inactivity budgets: prove a throttled, incompressible transfer completes byte-for-byte and receives its durable acknowledgement after running longer than the inactivity interval, through both the legacy and context APIs; stop the real receiver's transfer progress and assert bounded failure with the source retained, then prove caller deadline, cancellation and Close terminate and join an active transfer, and a delayed or failed durability acknowledgement cannot report success. Retain the assertions in TestSSHSession_Rsync at :63 and TestSSHSession_CancelTransfer at :118, including retry after receiver restart."
